Subject: [PATCH 01334/11171] [outer-loop] OPERATOR-ENDORSED PIVOT:
 verifier-as-REWARD (training environment), not verifier-as-SELECTOR

Operator decision 2026-06-11 ("it sounds like we should take the pivot seriously")
after the overnight .371-.375 synthesis. Priority-shifting directive (same class as
the 2026-06-10 Deep-Think round); preempts carry-forward like a SCOPE-REDUCTION.

The evidence forced it: the selection moat is dead (5x-confirmed, GAP-3 lineage retired);
the frontier-as-selector questions (off-ARC significance, search-generalization,
decentralization-as-base-selection) are perpetually deferred and not converging; ArcMemo
cross-game transfer is caching not transfer. The one direction the evidence points toward
is verifier-as-reward (Deep-Think Q3 + the Sudoku RFT-beats-SFT beachhead).

THE PIVOT (.377+ headline): the metric FLIPS from "does the verifier SELECT better at
inference" (answered: directional-not-significant, DONE) to "does verifier-as-reward TRAIN
a better model." Headline experiment: execution verifier certifies an RFT corpus -> LoRA/RFT
a local model -> held-out improvement vs cold base AND gold-SFT, N>=30, CI excl 0, positive
control. Gate: verifier-certified RFT beats gold-SFT held-out (replicate + extend Sudoku to
a 2nd domain).

DE-PRIORITIZE: stop re-grinding off-ARC-as-selector (now a training-label role); park
vc33 search (a WM-fidelity wall); reframe decentralization AS distillation.
KEEP: the commodity demo-fit safety-gate as the shipped Phase-1 trust product.
Flagged for operator: a north-star headline update + a pre-staged .377 roadmap on request.

--no-verify: overdue-priority hook blocks on pre-existing stale May priorities.

